Common facts about the Pekko breaker used by several stories (all read in `CB`):
- Transitions are `compareAndSwap` on the state object (700-704); only the thread that wins runs `enter()`. Listeners are notified after `_enter` (950-953) by `executor.execute(listener)` (844), i.e. asynchronously on the constructor ExecutionContext, with no ordering guarantee between listeners or against the caller's future.
- `callThrough` (857-908) has two paths. `callTimeout == Duration.Zero` (863-875): no timer, `defineFailureFn` and the allowlist are NOT consulted, any `Failure` is a failure. Otherwise (877-906) a `Promise` `p` is completed once by whichever of body or timer wins; failure counting is decided once in `p.future.onComplete` (881-888) by `defineFailureFn`.
- All CBSpec tests that exercise time are tagged `TimingTest` and use the real scheduler and sleeps. No spec drives the breaker with a manual scheduler.

